# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots the APISIX admin API in the BACKGROUND with the
# well-known DEFAULT admin key active, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the service is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable default key when the
#     agent starts;
#   * the admin key is read ONLY at process start, so changing the key file
#     without RESTARTING the service leaves the default key live — the
#     "fixed config but never restarted" case is detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting the service cannot kill the box.
